olivia-cs: FYI onboarding failure: Android app rollout causing a burst of 401s then 429s during SDK.init. ~260 devices after update.

max-platform: Thanks. SDK version + token type?

olivia-cs: android-sdk 1.4.0, ephemeral tokens from their /session endpoint. Logs:

```
W/AndroidHttp: POST /v1/respond 401 auth_missing
W/AndroidHttp: fetch /session
W/AndroidHttp: POST /v1/respond 429 rate_limit window=60s
```

Pattern: token requests then immediate generates without waiting.

tess-eng: Classic token-stampede + retry amplification. Short checklist: (1) ensure app awaits token promise before calling generate, (2) serialize SDK.init with a single entrypoint, (3) inject Authorization per-request via interceptor, (4) change retry-on-401 to refresh+single-replay with jittered backoff.

julia-support: KB snippet we give customers (Android):

```
// single-init guard
private final AtomicBoolean initGuard = new AtomicBoolean(false);
if (initGuard.compareAndSet(false, true)) {
  executor.execute(() -> {
    String tok = blockingFetchToken();
    Thread.sleep(ThreadLocalRandom.current().nextInt(200,1200)); // small jitter
    RedwoodSdk.initWithToken(context, tok);
    initGuard.set(false);
  });
}
// OkHttp interceptor to add header per request
```

max-platform: Short-term server-side smoothing: have their token endpoint reuse a recent ephemeral token for a short window (2-5s) or gate issuance behind a tiny semaphore. Also we should add a short onboarding note for mobile init patterns.

tess-eng: Recommend SDK config knobs: maxPreflightConcurrency=3, preflightCoalesce=true, tokenRefreshJitterMs=1000, retryOn401=false (do refresh+replay). Also upgrade to 1.4.1 which fixes a token-race.

alert-bot: [metric-alert] edge.rate.ignite spike -> 429s +410% in 5m.

olivia-cs: Customer applied single-init guard + 1s jitter + reduced preflight concurrency. They report 429s back to baseline. Closing loop; I'll add a short onboarding checklist item. Thanks everyone :thumbsup:
